-- title:
--   Ordinary Frobenius line in the Tate module of J₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $p$ be a prime with $p\nmid M$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain which is a $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra, with fraction field $K$, the $\mathbb Z_p$-algebra structures on $O$ and $K$ being compatible, and assume $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$. Equip $J_1(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with the module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129) over $\mathrm{HeckeAlgOne}=\mathbb Z[X_s : s\in \mathrm{Primes}\sqcup\mathbb N]$, and write $T=\mathrm{TateModule}\,p\,J_1(M)$ for the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_1(M)$ with $p^n x_n=0$ and $p\,x_{n+1}=x_n$. Let $\Lambda$ be a ring homomorphism from `rationalHeckeAlgebraOne`, the $\mathbb Q_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb Q_p}(\mathbb Q_p\otimes T)$ generated by the image of $\mathrm{HeckeAlgOne}$, to $K$, sending each $c\in\mathbb Z_p$ to its image in $K$. Let $a,d\in O$ with $a$ a unit, $\Lambda(T_p)=a$ and $\Lambda(\langle p\rangle)\,d=1$ in $K$, where $T_p$ and $\langle p\rangle$ denote `rationalHeckeOne` at the prime $p$ and `rationalDiamondOne` at $p$. Let $W$ be a $K$-vector space with $\dim_K W=2$, let $r$ be a map from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\mathrm{End}_K(W)$ (no multiplicativity assumed), and let $\pi\colon K\otimes_{\mathbb Z_p}T\to W$ be a surjective $K$-linear map intertwining the base change of the Galois action [`TateModule.rep`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L174) with $r$, and carrying the base change of each Hecke operator `tateHeckeRepOne p (JOne M) t` to multiplication by $\Lambda$ of the corresponding element `rationalHeckeRepOne p (JOne M) t`. Finally let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $P$. Then there is a $K$-submodule $L\subseteq W$ with $\dim_K L\le 1$ such that $r\sigma$ maps $L$ into $L$ for every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$; $r\tau\,w-w\in L$ for every $\tau$ in the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$ and every $w\in W$; and for every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup and acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{p}$, one has $r\sigma(r\sigma\,w)-(da)\,r\sigma\,w+(dp)\,w\in L$ for all $w\in W$.
--
--   This is the local behaviour at a good ordinary prime of the $p$-adic representation cut out on the Tate module of $J_1(M)$ by an ordinary Hecke character $\Lambda$: a line $L$ stable under the decomposition group at $P$, with inertia acting trivially on the quotient $W/L$, and with the Frobenius satisfying the Hecke polynomial $X^2-daX+dp$ modulo $L$ (for an eigenform of nebentypus $\varepsilon$, $da=a_p$ and $d=\varepsilon(p)$). It is used in the construction of the ordinary line and the unit-root Frobenius eigenvalue for the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a primitive form, via [`CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm.exists_galoisRepAdic_ordinaryLine_frobenius_sub_unitRoot_smul_mem_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsPrimitiveForm.exists_galoisRepAdic_ordinaryLine_frobenius_sub_unitRoot_smul_mem_of_not_dvd).
